 "total_bytes": 862015,
 "numbers": "VAL 1000 frames of 82 val scenes, GT v8 (signature 0.5_4_6a7aa7864a), EMA weights, cold memory, dt 0: board7 (mean of drivable IoU@0.5, walkway IoU@0, carpark IoU@0, ped crossing IoU@0, lane divider IoU@0.5, road divider IoU@1, det mAP) 0.45489 / 0.45482 (s0 / s1), mean 0.45486 (records/keep3.json); t23_C 0.44969 and t20_base_s0 0.44654 lie inside the band 0.02: a TIE by the metric, t21_ctl chosen by value by hand (2026-11-10). 102.5 ms per frame, idle GPU. Not SOA: behind GaussianCaR on the six map rows and behind CRN on objects (records/t26_g0/). The numbers are on GT v8; the live GT is v13 / v14 (t21_ctl not re-scored).",
 "command": "DOES NOT RUN AS IS: the code predates D76 and imports autogt (renamed GtGenerator, alias removed D78; D81: old runs are not run again); only the weights load under the live code (init_from). As it ran (ledger): bash temp/train/run_ar.sh temp/compose/t21_ctl_s0.json under run.py, config training/configs/t21_ctl.json (init_from runs/t20_base_s0/ckpt_00006000.pt, 1500 steps, lr 1e-4, warm-up 100, EMA 0.99, batch 3 x accum 2); evaluation then: bash temp/t21/eval_arm.sh runs/t21_ctl_s0; today's front door: python evaluation/evaluate.py runs/<run> --quant. Seed 1 ran at tag bf/t21.ctl_s1 (commit e544bdf063; the working tree changed while it ran). Alternative winner by role (the owner's choice): t20_base_s0 (tag bf/t20.base_s0, commit bd7eb0181b, board7 0.44654, one seed, the accepted reference baseline of D48).",
 "weights": "bev_fusion/runs/t21_ctl_s0/ckpt_00001500.pt (455,747,229 B) and runs/t21_ctl_s1/ckpt_00001500.pt (455,747,357 B), sha256 in records/keep3.json; warm-start parent runs/t20_base_s0/ckpt_00006000.pt; not in git"
